Let $R$ be commutative and $M$ an $R$-module. The following are equivalent:

1. $M$ is flat;
2. $\mathrm{Tor}_n^R(N,M) = 0$ for all $N$ and all $n\ge1$;
3. $\mathrm{Tor}_1^R(N,M) = 0$ for all $N$;
4. $\mathrm{Tor}_1^R(R/I,M) = 0$ for every ideal $I$, i.e. $I\otimes M\to M$ is injective for every ideal $I$.

Over $\mathbb{Z}$ (or any PID), a module is flat if and only if it is torsion-free.

Let $0\to N'\to N\to N''\to0$ be a short exact sequence of non-zero finitely generated $R$-modules. Then
1. $\operatorname{depth}N\ge\min\{\operatorname{depth}N',\operatorname{depth}N''\}$;
2. $\operatorname{depth}N''\ge\min\{\operatorname{depth}N,\operatorname{depth}N'-1\}$;
3. $\operatorname{depth}N'\ge\min\{\operatorname{depth}N,\operatorname{depth}N''+1\}$.
(Stacks Lemma 10.72.6.)
